{%- comment -%}
  YMAL — one product card, and THE eligibility gate.

  Every block renders through this, so the rule lives in exactly one file. An
  ineligible product renders as nothing at all, and the caller skips the gap.

  Usage:
    {%- render 'ymal-card', product: some_product, grid: 4 -%}

  `grid` is how many of these cards fit across the screen. It only sets the
  resolution asked of Shopify's image CDN - wider cards need a bigger source
  or they look soft - and never the displayed size, which is CSS. Optional,
  defaults to 4.

  `button_label` is the button's text. Optional, defaults to "Choose Option".
  It was the theme's own `quick_buy` translation, which reads "Quick Buy" here
  - a section setting is easier to change than a translation key.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Why this builds its own card instead of rendering the theme's product-block

  product-block is styled contextually - its rules assume it sits inside the
  theme's own product grid. Lifted into a different container it fell apart in
  ways that could not be overridden from outside: the price rendered beside the
  title rather than beneath it, even against id-scoped !important rules.

  So the markup here is ours and the layout is predictable. It still uses the
  theme's `image` and `price` snippets, so images are responsive and prices are
  formatted, localised and show sale styling exactly as everywhere else.

  What is given up: the hover-image swap, colour swatches, and the theme's
  stock labels. Those live in product-block and are not worth re-implementing
  for a recommendation strip.
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  The rule (docs/logic.md 4.1), as the storefront can see it:

  1. available    purchasable right now. Liquid knows this directly.
  2. not *SALE*   markdown. Liquid can read the title, so it is checked here as
                  well as in the metafield - it costs nothing and holds even if
                  the metafield is stale.
  3. eligible     stocked at Bali To Produce, so replenishable rather than
                  fixed. Liquid CANNOT compute this: it sees store-wide
                  inventory totals but never inventory by location. The
                  pipeline publishes it to product.metafields.ymal.eligible
                  (backend/scripts/publish_eligibility.py).

  FAILS CLOSED. No metafield means no card. "We have not checked" must not
  render as "fine to show" - that is the Wiser failure this project exists to
  fix. The visible cost is an empty block until the publish job has run, which
  is a problem someone notices.

  `.value`, not the metafield object: the object EXISTS even when it holds
  false, so testing it directly is truthy for an ineligible product and would
  fail open.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign ymal_eligible = product.metafields.ymal.eligible.value -%}

{%- assign ymal_is_sale = false -%}
{%- if product.title contains '*SALE*' -%}
  {%- assign ymal_is_sale = true -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if product.available and ymal_eligible and ymal_is_sale == false -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Wrapped in <product-block> so the theme's quick-buy works. Its script binds
    to that element and expects two things inside: a `.quickbuy-toggle` to
    click, and an empty `.quickbuy-container` to fill with the variant picker.
    Without the wrapper the button is just a link to the product page.

    Only the wrapper and those two hooks are borrowed - the card's own layout
    stays ours, because the theme's card styling assumes it sits inside the
    theme's product grid and falls apart elsewhere.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <product-block class="ymal-card" data-product-id="{{ product.id }}">
    <a class="ymal-card__link" href="{{ product.url }}">
      <div class="ymal-card__media">
        {%- if product.featured_media -%}
          {%- assign ymal_grid = grid | default: 4 -%}
          {%- render 'image' with product.featured_media.preview_image,
                loading: 'lazy',
                size_cols_mobile: 2,
                size_cols_desktop: ymal_grid,
                custom_crop: 'cover' -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <div class="ymal-card__title">{{ product.title | escape }}</div>

      <div class="ymal-card__price">
        {%- render 'price', product: product, show_labels: true -%}
      </div>
    </a>

    {%- comment -%}
      `quickbuy-toggle` opens the theme's variant picker. The href is a real
      product link, so the button still works if that script never runs - and
      gift cards skip it, as the theme's own card does.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- unless product.tags contains 'gift card' -%}
      <a class="ymal-card__button quickbuy-toggle" href="{{ product.url }}">
        {{ button_label | default: 'Choose Option' }}
      </a>

      <div class="quickbuy-container use-color-scheme use-color-scheme--{{ settings.quickbuy_color_scheme }}">
        <a href="#" class="close-detail" aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close' | t }}" tabindex="-1">
          {%- render 'icon-close', stroke_width: 1 -%}
        </a>
        <div class="inner"></div>
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
      <a class="ymal-card__button" href="{{ product.url }}">
        {{ button_label | default: 'Choose Option' }}
      </a>
    {%- endunless -%}
  </product-block>
{%- endif -%}
